"வல்","parts":[{"text":"வல்","lemma":"வல்","gloss":"strong/capable"}],"gloss":"capable"},{"surface":"சிறாஅர்","parts":[{"text":"சிறாஅர்","lemma":"சிறாஅர்","gloss":"young apprentices"}],"gloss":"young apprentices","split_unverified":true}]},{"words":[{"surface":"மழு","parts":[{"text":"மழு","lemma":"மழு","gloss":"axe"}],"gloss":"axe"},{"surface":"உடை","parts":[{"text":"உடை","lemma":"உடை","gloss":"possessing"}],"gloss":"possessing"},{"surface":"காட்டகத்து","parts":[{"text":"காட்டகத்து","lemma":"காட்டகத்து","gloss":"inside the forest"}],"gloss":"inside the forest","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"அற்றே","parts":[{"text":"அற்று","lemma":"அற்று","gloss":"like that"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"like that indeed"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"எத்திசை","parts":[{"text":"எ","lemma":"எ","gloss":"which"},{"text":"திசை","lemma":"திசை","gloss":"direction"}],"gloss":"whichever direction"},{"surface":"செலினும்","parts":[{"text":"செல்","lemma":"செல்","gloss":"go"},{"text":"இனும்","lemma":"இனும்","gloss":"even if"}],"gloss":"even if we go"},{"surface":"அத்திசை","parts":[{"text":"அ","lemma":"அ","gloss":"that"},{"text":"திசை","lemma":"திசை","gloss":"direction"}],"gloss":"that direction"},{"surface":"சோறே","parts":[{"text":"சோறு","lemma":"சோறு","gloss":"food/rice"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"food indeed"}]}],"literal":"O gatekeeper! O gatekeeper! / Sowing clear words in the ears of the generous, they / with a strong mind that accomplishes what was thought, / in this life of seeking gifts, suffering for honor, / O gatekeeper who does not close the gate to seekers of gifts! / Neṭumāṉ Añci, the lord of swift horses, / does he not know himself? Does he not know me? / Because those who possess wisdom and fame have died, / this world has not become an empty place; therefore, / we have carried our lute, we have packed our tool bag; / like the skilled young apprentices of a wood-cutting carpenter / who go into a forest with axes, / whichever direction we go, in that direction is our food!","translation":"O gatekeeper! O gatekeeper! You who never close the gates to seekers of gifts, who suffer for their honor in this life of seeking, sowing clear words in the ears of the generous to accomplish what they have resolved with strong minds! Does Neṭumāṉ Añci, the lord of swift horses, not know his own limits? Does he not know my worth? Just because those with wisdom and fame have passed away, this world has not become empty. Therefore, we have slung our lutes on our shoulders and packed our tool bags. Like the skilled young apprentices of a wood-cutting carpenter entering a forest with axes, whichever direction we go, in that direction we shall find our food!","modern":"வாயிற்காவலனே! வாயிற்காவலனே! வள்ளல்களின் காதுகளில் தெளிவான சொற்களை விதைத்து, தாம் நினைத்ததை முடிக்கும் வலிமையான நெஞ்சத்தோடு, மானத்திற்காக வருந்தும் பரிசில் வாழ்க்கை உடைய இரவலர்களுக்குக் கதவை அடைக்காத வாயிற்காவலனே! வேகமான குதிரைகளை உடைய தலைவனான நெடுமான் அஞ்சி, தன் பெருமையை அறியவில்லையா? என் தகுதியை அறியவில்லையா? அறிவும் புகழும் உடையவர்கள் இறந்துவிட்டதால் இந்த உலகம் வறுமையடைந்துவிடவில்லை. அதனால், யாழ்களைத் தோளில் மாட்டிக்கொண்டோம்; கருவிகள் உள்ள பையைச் சுருக்கிக் கட்டிக்கொண்டோம். மரம் வெட்டும் தச்சனின் தொழில் வல்ல சிறுவர்கள் கோடரியோடு காட்டிற்குள் செல்வது போல, நாங்கள் எந்தத் திசைக்குச் சென்றாலும் அந்தத் திசையில் எங்களுக்கு உணவு கிடைக்கும்.","explanation":"The poet Avvaiyār is speaking to the gatekeeper of King Atiyamāṉ Neṭumāṉ Añci. She has waited a long time for a gift from the king, and feeling insulted by his delay, she decides to leave. She proudly asserts the self-respect and capability of poets, comparing them to skilled carpenters. Just as a carpenter's apprentices with axes can find wood in any forest, talented poets can find patronage and livelihood wherever they go. The poem beautifully captures the pride, independence, and resilience of classical Tamil bards who refused to compromise their dignity for royal favors.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.4],[0.4,0.8],[0.8,1.42],[1.42,1.86],[1.86,2.3],[2.3,2.8],[2.8,3.4],[3.4,3.8],[3.8,4.8],[4.8,5.1],[5.1,5.3],[5.3,5.7],[5.7,7.2],[7.2,7.7],[7.7,8.1],[8.1,8.49],[8.49,9.5],[9.5,9.8],[9.8,10.1],[10.1,10.5],[10.5,11.0],[11.0,11.5],[11.5,12.0],[12.0,12.6],[12.6,13.12],[13.12,13.78],[13.78,14.3],[14.3,14.6],[14.6,14.9],[14.9,15.2],[15.2,15.5],[15.5,15.8],[17.88,18.48],[18.48,18.68],[18.68,19.18],[19.18,19.58],[19.58,20.15],[20.15,20.58],[20.58,21.58],[21.58,21.78],[21.78,22.98],[22.98,23.28],[23.28,23.78],[23.78,24.28],[24.28,24.78],[24.78,25.28],[25.28,25.8],[25.8,26.68],[26.68,26.88],[26.88,27.18],[27.18,27.58]],"female":[[0.0,0.5],[0.5,1.0],[1.0,1.3],[1.3,2.3],[2.3,3.3],[3.3,3.9],[3.9,4.67],[4.67,5.0],[5.0,6.1],[6.1,6.5],[6.5,6.7],[6.7,7.2],[7.2,8.8],[8.8,9.1],[9.1,10.1],[10.1,10.5],[10.5,11.6],[11.6,12.0],[12.0,12.2],[12.2,12.7],[12.7,13.35],[13.35,14.0],[14.0,14.5],[14.5,15.3],[15.3,15.8],[15.8,16.8],[16.8,17.15],[17.15,17.38],[17.5,18.7],[18.7,19.0],[19.0,19.7],[19.7,19.9],[20.96,21.56],[21.56,21.86],[21.86,22.46],[22.46,22.96],[22.96,23.7],[23.7,24.26],[24.26,25.36],[25.36,25.66],[25.66,26.96],[26.96,27.22],[27.22,27.66],[27.66,28.06],[28.06,28.56],[28.56,29.16],[29.16,29.31],[29.36,31.16],[31.16,31.46],[31.46,31.76],[31.76,32.46]]},"sync":[[["வாயிலோயே","O gatekeeper"]],[["வாயிலோயே","O gatekeeper"]],[["வாயிலோயே","O gatekeeper"]],[["வள்ளியோர்","generous people"]],[["செவி","ear"],["முதல்","at/near"]],[["வயங்கு","shining/clear"],["மொழி","words"]],[["வித்தி","having sown"],["தாம்","themselves"]],[["தாம்","themselves"]],[["உள்ளியது","that which was thought"]],[["முடிக்கும்","accomplishing"]],[["உரன்","strength"],["உடை","possessing"]],[["உள்ளத்து","of the mind"]],[["வரிசைக்கு","for honor"]],[["வருந்தும்","suffering"],["இ","this"],["பரிசில்","gift"]],[["பரிசில்","gift"]],[["வாழ்க்கை","life"]],[["பரிசிலர்க்கு","to the seekers of gifts"]],[["அடையா","not closing"]],[["வாயிலோயே","O gatekeeper"]],[["வாயிலோயே","O gatekeeper"]],[["கடு","swift"],["மான்"